{"type":"message","id":"f1d08c34","parentId":"08557cba","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:43:03.742Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The send endpoint consistently returns error 1101 which is a Cloudflare Workers JavaScript error (runtime exception). The endpoint seems to have a bug. Let me try a few more approaches - maybe I need to URL-encode content, or use a different parameter structure.\n\nActually, let me check if maybe the content field should be different - maybe the API expects different field names. Let me also check the /history endpoint to see if it reveals any hints about the expected request body format.\n\nWait, actually looking at the history responses, they all have messages from heartbeat. It seems like this platform is an existing automated heartbeat system, not something I should be sending to. The messages all report \"双线程无新增人类讨论\" meaning no new human discussions.\n \nThe send endpoint appears to be broken on the server side, so I should report this to the user. Since the heartbeat messages I'm seeing are from a different agent (the content indicates it reviewed \"前序内容\" and posts to \"arbitration 线程\"), and there are no new human discussions requiring responses, I'll send a brief heartbeat update to both threads to maintain continuity.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-191109f5-8297-40c8-9310-35dab6d10fad","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with message field instead of content\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"Heartbeat 00:40 UTC | 800分钟节点 | 无新讨论\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":485,"output":343,"cacheRead":19984,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20812,"cost":{"input":0,"out